    "title": "JSON schema for NuGet project.json files",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "description": "Our application targets both .NET\u202f5.0 and .NET\u202fStandard\u202f2.0 and relies on a few core NuGet packages. At the solution level we reference **Newtonsoft.Json** version\u202f13.0.1, **Serilog** version\u202f2.10.0 (using the default dependency type), and **Microsoft.Net.Compilers** version\u202f3.9.0 as a build\u2011time dependency. For the .NET\u202f5.0 framework we additionally pull in **Microsoft.Extensions.Logging** version\u202f5.0.0 and specify an import of\u202fdotnet5.0, while the .NET\u202fStandard\u202f2.0 profile brings in **System.Collections.Immutable** version\u202f5.0.0 and requires no special imports.\n\nThe runtime configuration is limited to three platforms: a 64\u2011bit Windows environment (win\u2011x64), a 64\u2011bit Linux Mint\u202f18 distribution (linuxmint.18\u2011x64), and a 64\u2011bit macOS\u202f10.12 system (osx.10.12\u2011x64). Accordingly, the project declares support for both net5.0 and netstandard2.0 target frameworks.",
  "reference_json": {
    "dependencies": {
      "Newtonsoft.Json": "13.0.1",
      "Serilog": {
        "version": "2.10.0",
        "type": "default"
      },
      "Microsoft.Net.Compilers": {
        "version": "3.9.0",
        "type": "build"
      }
    },
    "frameworks": {
      "net5.0": {
        "dependencies": {
          "Microsoft.Extensions.Logging": "5.0.0"
        },
        "imports": "dotnet5.0"
      },
      "netstandard2.0": {
        "dependencies": {
          "System.Collections.Immutable": "5.0.0"
        },
        "imports": ""
      }
    },
    "runtimes": {
      "win-x64": {},
      "linuxmint.18-x64": {},
      "osx.10.12-x64": {}
    },
    "supports": {
      "net5.0": {},
      "netstandard2.0": {}
    }
  }
}